"The Velras are a multigenerational Anesidoran family that collects the Chainer class."
"Each member selects different high-level wordchains from the System and shares them."
"They persuade Chainers to marry in, bind others by magical contract and adopt a few."
"They have four S-ranks, almost none of them active superheroes."
"Prominent Velras work for the Anesidoran government or sit on elite battle squads."
"They have as many friends as enemies among island Avowed, and are called the perennial champs."
"Aulia Velra, an S-rank, heads the family; her son Corin owns a big mansion on Anesidora."
"Keiko Velra, an A-rank Chainer hero in Tokyo for 15 years, is the family's rogue."
"Bedlam Beldam is a big supporter of the Velras."
"The family's System line refuses calls from unregistered selectees as unauthorized."
"Velras chant wordchains collectively, pooling their chains."
"The family lines up Chainer classes and passes them between members as grace periods end."
"A Velra who fails to get Chainer is not quite part of the family proper."
"Velras are raised in private schools; about two dozen have signed a family NDA."
"No Velra has ever died during a summons."
